v7
------------------------------------------
V7 is a JavaScript engine written in C. It makes it possible to program
Internet of Things (IoT) devices in JavaScript.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libv7-devel-3.0-1bl3
  libv7_3-3.0-1bl3
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/cesanta/v7

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/cesanta/v7/archive/refs/tags/3.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack v7-3.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./v7-3.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/v7-3.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/v7-3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libv7_3-3.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libv7-devel-3.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(v7)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/v7.README
  /usr/share/doc/v7/CONTRIBUTING.md
  /usr/share/doc/v7/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/v7/README.md
  /usr/share/doc/v7/ReleaseNotes.md

(libv7_3)
  /usr/bin/cygv7-3.dll

(libv7-devel)
  /usr/include/v7.h
  /usr/lib/libv7.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/v7.pc

